%% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
%% CAPTION
%%
%% What this shows: the whole pipeline, from published datasets on the left to
%% a prediction surface on the right, annotated with what is actually true
%% today rather than what is planned.
%%
%% Two of the thirteen queued sources are wired. Source 01 contributes 36
%% box-core rows that fan out into 108 records (one per evidence class);
%% source 05 contributes 1,658 individual nodule measurements that aggregate
%% DOWN to 72 event-level records. Deduplication then recognises that both
%% describe the same 36 box-core events and merges 05's records into 01's --
%% which is why the finished corpus is 108 rows from what looks like two
%% sources. Source 05 is not lost: its mean-nodule-mass values survive inside
%% the merged rows, and the manifest still lists it as a contributing source.
%%
%% Three sources are deliberately not wired. 06 and 18 were removed because
%% their stand-in files were fabricated placeholders, and a fabricated row has
%% no place in a citable corpus. 19 is queued but waits on the GRADE join
%% parameter. The corpus is single-source until Isaac delivers.
%%
%% Why it matters: the 108 and the 35 are different numbers and both are
%% correct. 108 rows are in the corpus; only 35 can train a model, because
%% only MASS rows with a valid abundance and a clean quality status qualify.
%% Anything that changes either number should be visible here.
%%
